{
 "source": "Kenney city, car, furniture, mini-character and modular-building kits (kenney.nl) and Quaternius Downtown City MegaKit, free Standard tier (quaternius.com)",
 "license": "CC0 1.0 Universal, both packs. Kenney's License.txt and Quaternius' License_Standard.txt are kept beside the meshes they cover.",
 "note": "A curated *scatter* library: the composer builds one scatter layer per entry and caps a world at 64, so this file is a short list on purpose -- glowmere.manifest.json is 13 entries for the same reason. The other ~900 meshes imported alongside these (buildings, roads, the downtown modules, furniture, the concert stage, the instruments, the rigged characters) are on disk and load fine, but they are placed by hand in a scene by file, the way assets/imported/alien.gltf is, because a building is not something you scatter by density. assets/imported/ATTRIBUTION.md lists every pack and where it came from. The scales here are av-gen's own art direction and they are the point of the file: Kenney's kit is modelled on a 1x1 unit tile with a 0.79-unit person and Quaternius' downtown reaches 28 units, neither of which is metres. preferredScale states the height in metres an instance wants, so a Kenney sedan and a Quaternius tower stand on the same street at the same scale.",
